`oodac tokens` of 05 (kinds only):

```
IDENT println  LPAREN  LPAREN  INT 1  RPAREN  COMMA  IDENT tok  RPAREN
```

Host walker skips the first `LPAREN`, then hits the grouping `RPAREN`
and stops. `tok` is never a refuse candidate. That is the wave-2/3
hole. This ELF still has it.

`main.oo` `run` **does** call `run_check_core` first. The front-door
FN is what lets `run` execute. `emit-bc` still skips check (s29 R-bc).

