3. Source (WT) — what a rebuild *would* run
---

`check_secret_println_sinks` L185–211 (WT; **not** in this ELF):

```
if sid == "println" || sid == "eprintln" {
    … optional one LPAREN …
    let mut depth = 1;
    while in_args && p < n {
        if tk == "LPAREN" { depth = depth + 1; p = p + 1; }
        else if tk == "RPAREN" {
            depth = depth - 1;
            if depth <= 0 { in_args = false; }
            p = p + 1;
        } else if tk == "IDENT" {
            c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved(env, sid, nm);
```

`c_secret_scan_call` L109–125: same depth; `COMMA` only if `depth == 1`.

`c_emit_println` L19–33: `d` on LPAREN / RPAREN so `("x") + tok` is
still one arg and `tok` is a refuse candidate.

**Still no** `c_secret_emit_guard` in `c_emit_secret.oo` /
`c_emit_print.oo` / `c_emit_ident.oo` (grep **none**). Wave-3 is not
DE2.9. After a rebuild that actually links this `.oo`, check / llvm /
wasm / run / emit-c **front-door** should refuse 05/06/08/09.

---
4. Runtime (`chs_rt`) — not a SECRET host
---

`chs_rt_print.c`: `oo_print_str` / `oo_println` / `oo_eprintln` write
stdout/stderr. **No** taint, **no** `ERR\tsecret`.

`oodac run` of 05 printing `1` is a **front-door miss**, not a runtime
seal miss.

